    <item>
      <title>App Intelligence access reviews documented alongside revised Trim Versions guidance — 11 November 2026</title>
      <link>https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-11/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-11/</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:15:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <description><![CDATA[<div style="max-width:760px;color:#11181d;font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><div style="margin:0 0 24px"><div style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.3 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase">Day in brief · 11 November 2026</div><h2 style="margin:0 0 12px;font:650 28px/1.2 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-11/" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">App Intelligence access reviews documented alongside revised Trim Versions guidance</a></h2><p style="margin:0;color:#263030;font:16px/1.6 Arial,sans-serif">The November 11 period was documentation-led: Microsoft added a SharePoint governance article describing how administrators can prioritize and investigate non-Microsoft application access, and revised Trim Versions guidance with clearer operational limits and procedures.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/assets/products/sharepoint.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/assets/topics/governance.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">SharePoint · Permissions and governance</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-11/#doc-2026-11-11-review-application-access-with-app-intelligence-sharepoint-in-microsoft-365-01" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">New workflow covers non-Microsoft application access investigations</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">The new SharePoint article explains how administrators can prioritize and investigate application access using permissions, site reach, behavior evidence, and privileged-access information. Availability, required roles, licensing, and assessment data vary by tenant and release.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/assets/products/content-management.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/assets/topics/general.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Content and versions · General</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-11/#doc-2026-11-11-trim-versions-02" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Trim Versions guidance now emphasizes the 30-day minimum</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">The revised article identifies SharePoint Administrators as able to queue trim jobs, simplifies What-if and manual-expiration guidance, highlights the 30-day minimum, and removes the previous text about versions created before January 1, 2023.</p></div><p style="margin:24px 0 0"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-11/" style="color:#0d5745;font:700 15px/1.4 Georgia,serif">View all updates for 11 November 2026 →</a></p></div>]]></description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<div style="max-width:760px;color:#11181d;font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><div style="margin:0 0 24px"><div style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.3 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase">Day in brief · 11 November 2026</div><h2 style="margin:0 0 12px;font:650 28px/1.2 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-11/" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">App Intelligence access reviews documented alongside revised Trim Versions guidance</a></h2><p style="margin:0;color:#263030;font:16px/1.6 Arial,sans-serif">The November 11 period was documentation-led: Microsoft added a SharePoint governance article describing how administrators can prioritize and investigate non-Microsoft application access, and revised Trim Versions guidance with clearer operational limits and procedures.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/assets/products/sharepoint.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/assets/topics/governance.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">SharePoint · Permissions and governance</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-11/#doc-2026-11-11-review-application-access-with-app-intelligence-sharepoint-in-microsoft-365-01" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">New workflow covers non-Microsoft application access investigations</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">The new SharePoint article explains how administrators can prioritize and investigate application access using permissions, site reach, behavior evidence, and privileged-access information. Availability, required roles, licensing, and assessment data vary by tenant and release.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/assets/products/content-management.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/assets/topics/general.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Content and versions · General</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-11/#doc-2026-11-11-trim-versions-02" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Trim Versions guidance now emphasizes the 30-day minimum</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">The revised article identifies SharePoint Administrators as able to queue trim jobs, simplifies What-if and manual-expiration guidance, highlights the 30-day minimum, and removes the previous text about versions created before January 1, 2023.</p></div><p style="margin:24px 0 0"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-11/" style="color:#0d5745;font:700 15px/1.4 Georgia,serif">View all updates for 11 November 2026 →</a></p></div>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Teams events will share OneDrive videos directly without screen sharing — 10 November 2026</title>
      <link>https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-10/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-10/</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:15:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <description><![CDATA[<div style="max-width:760px;color:#11181d;font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><div style="margin:0 0 24px"><div style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.3 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase">Day in brief · 10 November 2026</div><h2 style="margin:0 0 12px;font:650 28px/1.2 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-10/" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Teams events will share OneDrive videos directly without screen sharing</a></h2><p style="margin:0;color:#263030;font:16px/1.6 Arial,sans-serif">The period’s main product update is a planned Microsoft Teams events capability that lets organizers and producers share OneDrive videos through “Manage what attendees see.” A separate SharePoint app-bar guidance update adds detail on navigation features, requirements, Teams integration, and rollout timing.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/assets/products/sharepoint.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/assets/topics/governance.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">SharePoint · Permissions and governance</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-10/#MC1506734" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">OneDrive video sharing in Teams events</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">Microsoft Teams will let event organizers and producers share videos directly from OneDrive using “Manage what attendees see,” avoiding screen sharing or embedding videos in PowerPoint and supporting smoother, higher-quality playback. Rollout begins in mid-November 2026, with no action required.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/assets/products/sites.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/assets/topics/architecture.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Sites and intranet · Planning and deployment</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-10/#doc-2026-11-10-set-up-global-navigation-in-the-sharepoint-app-bar-sharepoint-in-microsoft-365-01" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Global navigation guidance adds feature and rollout detail</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">The SharePoint app-bar setup page now describes personalized favorites and recents, quick access to Discover, Publish, Build, and OneDrive, and clarifies global-navigation requirements, permissions, Teams integration, and the possible 24-hour rollout delay.</p></div><p style="margin:24px 0 0"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-10/" style="color:#0d5745;font:700 15px/1.4 Georgia,serif">View all updates for 10 November 2026 →</a></p></div>]]></description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<div style="max-width:760px;color:#11181d;font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><div style="margin:0 0 24px"><div style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.3 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase">Day in brief · 10 November 2026</div><h2 style="margin:0 0 12px;font:650 28px/1.2 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-10/" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Teams events will share OneDrive videos directly without screen sharing</a></h2><p style="margin:0;color:#263030;font:16px/1.6 Arial,sans-serif">The period’s main product update is a planned Microsoft Teams events capability that lets organizers and producers share OneDrive videos through “Manage what attendees see.” A separate SharePoint app-bar guidance update adds detail on navigation features, requirements, Teams integration, and rollout timing.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/assets/products/sharepoint.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/assets/topics/governance.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">SharePoint · Permissions and governance</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-10/#MC1506734" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">OneDrive video sharing in Teams events</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">Microsoft Teams will let event organizers and producers share videos directly from OneDrive using “Manage what attendees see,” avoiding screen sharing or embedding videos in PowerPoint and supporting smoother, higher-quality playback. Rollout begins in mid-November 2026, with no action required.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/assets/products/sites.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/assets/topics/architecture.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Sites and intranet · Planning and deployment</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-10/#doc-2026-11-10-set-up-global-navigation-in-the-sharepoint-app-bar-sharepoint-in-microsoft-365-01" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Global navigation guidance adds feature and rollout detail</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">The SharePoint app-bar setup page now describes personalized favorites and recents, quick access to Discover, Publish, Build, and OneDrive, and clarifies global-navigation requirements, permissions, Teams integration, and the possible 24-hour rollout delay.</p></div><p style="margin:24px 0 0"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-10/" style="color:#0d5745;font:700 15px/1.4 Georgia,serif">View all updates for 10 November 2026 →</a></p></div>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Sensitivity-labeled PDFs gain web annotation in OneDrive and SharePoint in January 2027 — 9 November 2026</title>
      <link>https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-09/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-09/</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 08:15:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <description><![CDATA[<div style="max-width:760px;color:#11181d;font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><div style="margin:0 0 24px"><div style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.3 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase">Day in brief · 9 November 2026</div><h2 style="margin:0 0 12px;font:650 28px/1.2 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-09/" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Sensitivity-labeled PDFs gain web annotation in OneDrive and SharePoint in January 2027</a></h2><p style="margin:0;color:#263030;font:16px/1.6 Arial,sans-serif">OneDrive for Business and SharePoint on the web are scheduled to let users with editing rights annotate sensitivity-label protected PDFs without removing their labels. Saved files will retain both annotations and protections, with worldwide rollout planned for late January 2027.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/assets/products/sharepoint.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/assets/topics/general.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">SharePoint · General</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-09/#MC1545696" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Editing rights will include annotation of protected PDFs</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">Users with editing rights will be able to annotate sensitivity-label protected PDFs on the web without removing the labels. Annotations and protections will be preserved when the file is saved; worldwide rollout is planned for late January 2027.</p></div><p style="margin:24px 0 0"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-09/" style="color:#0d5745;font:700 15px/1.4 Georgia,serif">View all updates for 9 November 2026 →</a></p></div>]]></description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<div style="max-width:760px;color:#11181d;font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><div style="margin:0 0 24px"><div style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.3 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase">Day in brief · 9 November 2026</div><h2 style="margin:0 0 12px;font:650 28px/1.2 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-09/" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Sensitivity-labeled PDFs gain web annotation in OneDrive and SharePoint in January 2027</a></h2><p style="margin:0;color:#263030;font:16px/1.6 Arial,sans-serif">OneDrive for Business and SharePoint on the web are scheduled to let users with editing rights annotate sensitivity-label protected PDFs without removing their labels. Saved files will retain both annotations and protections, with worldwide rollout planned for late January 2027.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/assets/products/sharepoint.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/assets/topics/general.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">SharePoint · General</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-09/#MC1545696" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">Editing rights will include annotation of protected PDFs</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">Users with editing rights will be able to annotate sensitivity-label protected PDFs on the web without removing the labels. Annotations and protections will be preserved when the file is saved; worldwide rollout is planned for late January 2027.</p></div><p style="margin:24px 0 0"><a href="https://daily.sharepoint.admin.news/day/2026-11-09/" style="color:#0d5745;font:700 15px/1.4 Georgia,serif">View all updates for 9 November 2026 →</a></p></div>]]></content:encoded>
